Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: do not reconnect at the end of a chunked body

A response framed with Transfer-Encoding: chunked leaves s->filesize at
UINT64_MAX. When the connection is persistent (multiple_requests, which
the HLS demuxer sets on every playlist and segment it opens), the last
chunk sets s->chunkend and http_buf_read() reports the completed body as
AVERROR_EOF. http_read_stream() then tests for a premature end with
`s->off < s->filesize`, which is true of every chunked response, and --
with reconnect enabled -- treats the clean end as a dropped connection.

The reconnect never recovers: http_connect() resets every per-response
field except chunkend, so the very first read on the new connection is
AVERROR_EOF again, and the loop walks its whole backoff (0, 1, 3, 7, 15,
31, 63, ... seconds, each a fresh GET of the same playlist) before
failing with EIO. For an HLS variant playlist that means no segment is
ever requested. Plezy hits this whenever a Plex custom access URL sits
behind a reverse proxy or tunnel that re-frames the playlist as chunked
(edde746/plezy#2406): PMS reached directly answers with Content-Length
and plays, the same title through the proxy spins forever. mpv
propagates the player's reconnect/reconnect_streamed options to every
nested HLS open, so the demuxer's persistent connections carry them.

Treat an EOF with chunkend set as the end it is, ahead of the streamed
and premature-end tests -- unless reconnect_at_eof asked for exactly
that reconnect -- and reset chunkend with the rest of the per-response
state in http_connect() so a later seek, request or reconnect_at_eof
reconnect on the same context does not start at EOF.

Verified on n8.0.1: a chunked HLS VOD served over a keep-alive connection
probes and plays with reconnect=1,reconnect_streamed=1 where it used to
re-request the playlist on the backoff schedule; Content-Length framing,
chunked without reconnect, and a genuinely truncated Content-Length body
(which still logs "Stream ends prematurely" and reconnects) behave as
before. Not upstream yet; drop this patch once the pinned FFmpeg carries
the fix.

diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -1604,6 +1604,7 @@ static int http_connect(URLContext *h, const char *path, const char *local_path,
     s->off              = 0;
     s->icy_data_read    = 0;
     s->filesize         = UINT64_MAX;
+    s->chunkend         = 0;
     s->willclose        = 0;
     s->end_chunked_post = 0;
     s->end_header       = 0;
@@ -1772,6 +1773,13 @@ static int http_read_stream(URLContext *h, uint8_t *buf, int size)
         if (read_ret == AVERROR_EXIT)
             break;
 
+        /* The last chunk of a persistent chunked response is the end of the
+         * body, not a dropped connection: filesize is unknown for chunked
+         * transfers, so the premature-end test below cannot tell them apart.
+         * reconnect_at_eof asks to reconnect at exactly this point. */
+        if (read_ret == AVERROR_EOF && s->chunkend && !s->reconnect_at_eof)
+            break;
+
         if (h->is_streamed && !s->reconnect_streamed)
             break;
 
